{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. The context inputs `N`, `K`, and `X` are not scored as observations, and both parameters have built-in priors before use.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Learning Physics from Dynamical Scenes
data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> K;
  matrix[N, K] X;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[K] beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  sigma ~ lognormal(0, 1);
  y ~ normal(X * beta, sigma);
}
generated quantities {
  vector[N] mu = X * beta;
}

